  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#relaxing-the-same-origin-restriction\r\n\r\n> If the given value is not a registrable domain suffix of and is not equal to effectiveDomain, then throw a \"SecurityError\" DOMException\\.\r\n\r\nI think the \"is a registrable domain suffix of or is equal to\" check is incorrect for this usage: it seems to calculate a public suffix (e.g. `com`), as opposed to a registrable domain (e.g. `example.com`). For `document.domain`, I think we need to broaden the definition to actually include the latter.",
